2. Current Admissible Claims

BAS Test 0 may currently claim only:

A simplified test configuration has been defined.
The test objective is bounded vertical oscillation of an HDPE drum under shallow-water conditions.
External pump energy is allowed only to restore buoyancy state.
Output extraction, efficiency, and power generation are outside scope.
Initial testing is limited to a 6-inch stroke.
Success, if observed, applies only to the locked Test 0 condition.

Admissible wording:

“BAS Test 0 is configured to test whether controlled buoyancy-state cycling can produce bounded repeated vertical motion under recorded 4 ft water-depth conditions.”

