Required evidence discipline:

log startup state,
record full runs,
preserve failed cycles,
report variance, not just averages,
separate clean runs from contaminated runs,
document pump timing and behavior,
document rod/bushing condition before and after,
classify intervention-contaminated runs explicitly.
8. Transition to Simulation Phase
Simulation is allowed to explore
expected stroke timing ranges,
sensitivity of Q_pump vs Q_leak,
restoration lag effects,
rod friction thresholds,
partial-fill and trapped-air sensitivity,
phase drift signatures,
rebound effects,
stroke-length sensitivity between 6 inches and 12 inches,
likely attractor/metastability/divergence signatures.
Simulation cannot validate
stable BAS behavior,
repeatability,
low-friction guide performance,
dirty-water viability,
pump restoration dominance,
absence of trapped-air problems,
absence of rod bind,
physical durability,
scalability,
operational readiness.
